Z||000016||87FieroGTx||07-30-2001||06:54 AM|||| I like Oreif's car but I HATE the snorkel, I've never understood them. They slow the car down and from what I hear actually HEAT up the engine bay.<P> FROM WHAT I HEAR <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> To cool the engine bay down you need to let more air in from under the engine and open up more holes on the top. When you put a snorkel on it disrupts the airflow and keeps the hot air in.<P> This info is from many article's I've read and I've experimented with both ways and the snorkel sucks for performance.<P> THE ONLY way I see for a snorkel to help with performance is to have the air intake hooked directly to it. Even then The drag would probably make the extra horsepower moot.||||reg||1
