Z||000021||Oreif||07-30-2001||01:59 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87FieroGTx:<BR><B> I like Oreif's car but I HATE the snorkel, I've never understood them. They slow the car down and from what I hear actually HEAT up the engine bay.<P> FROM WHAT I HEAR  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> To cool the engine bay down you need to let more air in from under the engine and open up more holes on the top. When you put a snorkel on it disrupts the airflow and keeps the hot air in.<P> This info is from many article's I've read and I've experimented with both ways and the snorkel sucks for performance.<P> THE ONLY way I see for a snorkel to help with performance is to have the air intake hooked directly to it. Even then The drag would probably make the extra horsepower moot.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The center mounted snorkel Forces air down the back side of the engine Aiding in cooling. As for ducting it into the engine, It uses the cooler air commonly referred to as "Clean Air" in the racing community.<BR>The drag from the sccop is moot because the scoop is designed to use the flow over the windshield/roof. For those that think the scoop will slow the car down, Just look at the wind tunnel tests done on the IMSA Fiero race car in the Pontiac Performance Plus Magazine that explains how they came up with the design. <P>As for the MR2 folks, They have their own opinion's. There are things they do to the MR2 that I think look silly. To each his own.<BR>I never asked them to like my car. <P>I wonder what they'll think of the new secret hood I am designing?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
